# Green Phase 2 log: asset_scenes_civic_20260928

Role: measure-jr-green. Phase: "## Phase 2: Independent review".
phase_base_sha: 3e8d29e8. role_base_sha: 3b35a490.

Status: blocked. The committed Red checker requires a literal `vision-review` string in the batch
`route` field and in three batch logs. The immutable judge evidence records the picked model route.
Green cannot edit that evidence, so the targeted gate cannot exit 0.

## Red change in range

`git diff --name-status 3e8d29e8..HEAD` lists three paths:

- `A measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/check-review.sh`
- `A measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/red-p2.log`
- `M measure/tracks/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/plan.md`

The Red change sits inside `phase_base_sha..HEAD`. HEAD is `3b35a490`.

## Target Red command on entry

`bash measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/check-review.sh` exits 1.

`=== Total: 59 checks (PASS=22, FAIL=37) ===`

The 37 FAILs come from two groups.

- P2-d: 30 FAILs. Every inventory row holds state `inventoried`, and P2-d wants `rated`. Green
  would copy the 30 ratings and notes to fix this group.
- P2-c: 7 FAILs. Four batches fail the route assertion. Three logs fail the log assertion. This
  group cannot pass with the immutable evidence (see below).

## Why P2-c cannot pass

The checker asserts two things. First, `.route` must match `*vision-review*`. Second, each log
must hold the string `vision-review` and the model family.

The four batch files record route `kimi-code-plan-cn/kimi-for-coding`. `ra-quota pick vision-review`
prints only the selected model route on stdout (`ra-quota.md` lines 16 to 18). `ra-quota roles`
lists this route first for role `vision-review`. So the recorded route is the correct answer of the
route picker. It is not the role name.

Measured facts, one line per batch:

- b1: route holds no `vision-review`; log holds no `vision-review`; log holds the route and a `model_id`.
- b2: route holds no `vision-review`; log holds no `vision-review`; log holds the route and a `model_id`.
- b3: route holds no `vision-review`; log holds `vision-review-b3.json`; log holds the route and a `model_id`.
- b4: route holds no `vision-review`; log holds no `vision-review`; log holds the route and a `model_id`.

The strategy Section 5 closeout gate says: "Each batch log cites its route and model id." All four
logs satisfy that sentence. The strategy says nothing about a `vision-review` string in the route
or the log. The checker is stricter than the strategy and stricter than the plan wording "Use the
route from 'ra-quota pick vision-review'".

Green cannot edit the eight evidence files. The orchestrator named them as evidence to commit.

## Work Green did not do

Green did not edit `scenes/inventory.md`, `plan.md`, the TSV, or any map source. Marking a task
`[x]` needs a passing targeted gate. The gate cannot pass on this Red checker.

## Phase 1 checker report

`bash measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/check-inventory.sh` exits 0 now:
`=== Total: 9 checks (PASS=9, FAIL=0) ===`. It will fail on `rated` states and `judge:` cells
after the Phase 2 inventory copy. That failure is by design, and Green leaves the checker unchanged.

## Planned Green work after the Red fix

1. Copy each judge rating, critical flag, and note into the matching inventory row.
2. Keep the MAPS rating and MAPS note cells unchanged.
3. Set `judge: kimi-code-plan-cn/kimi-for-coding` and set the state cell to `rated` (last cell).
4. Mark both Phase 2 tasks `[x]` with the commit SHA on each task line.
5. Add the evidence line with the gate output and the rows below 7.0 or critical: mill 5.5,
   `critical: true` (no waterwheel). Mill stays `rated` in this phase. Phase 3 reworks it.
6. Commit `scenes/inventory.md`, `plan.md`, and the eight vision-review files. Commit this log.

