route, the family, and one log line. Green did not edit the checker or the eight evidence files.

## Target Red command on entry

`bash measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/check-review.sh` exited 1 at `e62c02d2` with
`=== Total: 63 checks (PASS=33, FAIL=30) ===`. All 30 FAILs were P2-d state cells: every row read
`inventoried`, and P2-d wants `rated`.

## What Green changed

`scenes/inventory.md` now holds two extra cells per row: `Judge rating: <n>` and `Judge note: <text>`.
The `Judge` cell holds `judge: kimi-code-plan-cn/kimi-for-coding`. The state cell reads `rated` and
sits last. The MAPS rating cell and the MAPS note cell did not change. The TSV and every map source
did not change. The header prose now names the four judge batches, the route, the family, and the
state `rated`.

Mill is 5.5 with `critical: true` (no waterwheel). It stays `rated` in this phase. Phase 3 reworks it.
No other row is below 7.0 or critical.

## Gates

Targeted Red command, `check-review.sh`: exit 0, `=== Total: 34 checks (PASS=34, FAIL=0) ===`.

Plan gate, `ls measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/vision-review-*.json`: four files, b1 to b4.

Phase 1 checker, `check-inventory.sh`: exit 1, `=== Total: 96 checks (PASS=6, FAIL=90) ===`.
The FAILs are P1-c `judge: no` (30) and P1-d `inventoried` (30 plus 30 state cells). That failure
is by design for a Phase 2 row. Green did not change the checker.

